  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "eugr's (Eugene Rakhmatulin) spark-vllm-docker deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp recipe for DeepSeek's DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp (checkpoint revision 6821d6ad), MIT, served by vLLM on two Sparks. Runs eugr's published vllm-node-b12x image (nightly-20260929, `--exp-b12x` lane, digest pinned; its build-metadata records spark-vllm-docker 42f62e34 and the local-inference-lab/vllm dev/karmic-kraken vLLM fork with lukealonso's b12x kernels) with upstream's launch: B12X attention, MoE and linear backends, b12x load format, FP8 KV cache with block size 256, DSpark speculative decoding with 6 tokens (probabilistic draft sampling) using the checkpoint's own draft layers, deepseek_v4 tokenizer, tool-call and reasoning parsers with thinking on and high reasoning effort by default, full-and-piecewise CUDA graphs (capture size 48), eight sequences, 8,192 batched tokens and memory utilisation 0.85 (upstream defaults). Upstream sets max-model-len to `auto` and so does this recipe (vLLM picks the largest context that fits; the checkpoint's configured maximum is 1,048,576 tokens, recorded as the context setting but not bound to the launch). Upstream's `--default-chat-template-kwargs.thinking=true` and `.reasoning_effort=high` are passed as one JSON `--default-chat-template-kwargs` value (equivalent). Upstream's instanttensor-hybrid-draft-loader and drop-caches mods are commented out and not applied. The recipe is cluster-only upstream (two Sparks). No upstream performance claims are recorded. Upstream repository MIT. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
    "tags": [
      "b12x",
      "candidate",
      "deepseek",
      "deepseek-v4",
      "dspark",
      "dual",
      "eugr",
      "executable",
